1
00:00:05,506 --> 00:00:10,426
9 YEARS LATER
THE BLUE HOUSE, 1979

2
00:00:20,687 --> 00:00:22,064
Deputy Director Baek.

3
00:00:22,606 --> 00:00:23,607
Hello, sir.

4
00:00:24,274 --> 00:00:26,150
That's right. I'm Baek Kitae.

5
00:00:26,151 --> 00:00:28,820
The deputy director of
the Korean Central Intelligence Agency.

6
00:00:30,739 --> 00:00:32,491
So…

7
00:00:34,618 --> 00:00:36,662
…how long have I been in this chair?

8
00:00:37,371 --> 00:00:39,456
Almost… two decades.

9
00:00:40,791 --> 00:00:44,377
And that's far too long for this job,
isn't it?

10
00:00:44,378 --> 00:00:45,962
Absolutely not.

11
00:00:45,963 --> 00:00:47,130
Yes, it is.

12
00:00:48,340 --> 00:00:51,342
That's why there's been such a…
strident outcry.

13
00:00:51,343 --> 00:00:53,302
Don't worry about that.

14
00:00:53,303 --> 00:00:55,931
People love to raise their voices.
They'll all stop soon.

15
00:01:00,811 --> 00:01:02,395
On a separate subject,

16
00:01:02,396 --> 00:01:05,649
the way Director Cho's been
looking at me lately, well…

17
00:01:06,858 --> 00:01:08,235
it's different now.

18
00:01:08,860 --> 00:01:10,904
What's your opinion? You agree?

19
00:01:12,281 --> 00:01:14,407
Busan's dealing with the protests.

20
00:01:14,408 --> 00:01:16,659
I'd say that's putting him
in a tough position.

21
00:01:16,660 --> 00:01:18,578
President Park's left and right hands:

22
00:01:18,579 --> 00:01:23,165
Director Cho of the KCIA and Chief Gwak
of the Presidential Security Service.

23
00:01:23,166 --> 00:01:27,296
On the surface, they claim to be searching
for a solution to the unrest in Busan.

24
00:01:28,046 --> 00:01:30,923
But the truth is they're competing
for the president's favor

25
00:01:30,924 --> 00:01:32,842
and their share of the pie.

26
00:01:32,843 --> 00:01:35,387
The Yushin regime is autocratic
and tyrannical.

27
00:01:37,639 --> 00:01:39,600
That's what all the protestors are saying.

28
00:01:40,350 --> 00:01:43,144
And then there's Cheon Seokjung,
Park's Chief of Staff,

29
00:01:43,145 --> 00:01:45,688
and the second-most powerful man
in the country right now.

30
00:01:45,689 --> 00:01:47,899
Look, I'm sure they have their reasons.

31
00:01:48,734 --> 00:01:49,900
What?

32
00:01:49,901 --> 00:01:54,280
Things will only get worse if we decide
to suppress the demonstrations by force.

33
00:01:54,281 --> 00:01:58,409
See what I mean? The KCIA has
gone too damn soft for my taste.

34
00:01:58,410 --> 00:02:01,705
It's giving these commie protestors
whatever they want.

35
00:02:02,289 --> 00:02:04,624
I say let's just roll some tanks in there.

36
00:02:05,208 --> 00:02:07,501
And you, shut your mouth.

37
00:02:07,502 --> 00:02:10,504
What'd you say to me, you asshole? Huh?

38
00:02:10,505 --> 00:02:13,257
Come on, that's enough.
Don't be so vulgar.

39
00:02:13,258 --> 00:02:15,594
Oh, I think you heard me.

40
00:02:16,219 --> 00:02:17,638
Asshole!

41
00:02:18,138 --> 00:02:20,514
Hey, hey, cool it. Let's be civil here.

42
00:02:20,515 --> 00:02:23,059
- You little shit.
-  Whoa, here we go.

43
00:02:23,060 --> 00:02:25,353
- Have you lost your damn mind or what?
- Excuse me?

44
00:02:25,354 --> 00:02:27,938
You really want to push me over the line,
you asshole?

45
00:02:27,939 --> 00:02:29,732
You know, swearing won't fix the country.

46
00:02:29,733 --> 00:02:31,400
How dare you…

47
00:02:31,401 --> 00:02:32,860
I'm gonna crush you…

48
00:02:32,861 --> 00:02:35,488
Think you can get cocky
just 'cause the president's backing you?

49
00:02:35,489 --> 00:02:37,491
Think you're better than me,
you piece of shit?

50
00:02:38,450 --> 00:02:39,868
Cho's become too soft.

51
00:02:40,952 --> 00:02:43,205
The KCIA needs to crack down harder.

52
00:02:44,748 --> 00:02:47,000
- Don't you think?
- Absolutely, sir.

53
00:02:48,502 --> 00:02:50,419
Stick as close as you can to Cho.

54
00:02:50,420 --> 00:02:52,047
Keep an eye on him, my friend.

55
00:02:52,881 --> 00:02:54,465
Yes, sir.

56
00:02:59,012 --> 00:03:00,847
Mr. President, Madam Shin is here.

57
00:03:03,475 --> 00:03:06,478
Ah, there you are.
Glad you could make it, Madam Shin.

58
00:03:10,524 --> 00:03:13,693
I was feeling a little unsettled
after a strange dream.

59
00:03:17,239 --> 00:03:19,991
By the way, this is Baek Kitae,
the man I told you about.

60
00:03:20,575 --> 00:03:23,286
He's the deputy director of the KCIA.

61
00:03:24,955 --> 00:03:26,415
Introduce yourself.

62
00:03:28,458 --> 00:03:29,709
Baek Kitae, madam.

63
00:03:32,754 --> 00:03:34,464
You're very handsome.

64
00:03:37,926 --> 00:03:39,385
I'm Madam Shin.

65
00:03:47,894 --> 00:03:50,564
You have such lovely hands too.

66
00:03:59,656 --> 00:04:04,453
I can see why
you treasure him so dearly, sir.

67
00:04:06,663 --> 00:04:12,293
He'll lead this country
as the next KCIA director.

68
00:04:12,294 --> 00:04:14,546
At your service!
Thank you!

69
00:04:15,338 --> 00:04:19,092
Oh, wow.
So you speak a little Japanese as well?

70
00:04:21,011 --> 00:04:23,053
I lived in Osaka for a while.

71
00:04:23,054 --> 00:04:25,557
Ah, Osaka.

72
00:04:26,224 --> 00:04:27,225
Very nice.

73
00:04:28,769 --> 00:04:32,689
All right, Baek, keep a close watch
on Cho and report to me regularly.

74
00:04:33,315 --> 00:04:34,524
Of course, sir!

75
00:04:35,150 --> 00:04:37,986
I think it's time to go in, Madam Shin.

76
00:04:39,029 --> 00:04:40,197
'Cause I'm getting impatient.

77
00:04:41,531 --> 00:04:42,783
All right, let's go.

78
00:05:07,182 --> 00:05:09,226
So I'll be the director?

79
00:06:10,370 --> 00:06:12,788
That son of a bitch
has gone insane, I swear.

80
00:06:13,874 --> 00:06:16,250
He's not gonna get away with this.

81
00:06:16,251 --> 00:06:18,879
- Good afternoon, Director.
- Gonna smash his smug little face in.

82
00:06:20,088 --> 00:06:21,672
That bastard is dead.

83
00:06:21,673 --> 00:06:23,425
I'm gonna tear him to little pieces.

84
00:06:24,509 --> 00:06:25,594
What's the matter?

85
00:06:28,430 --> 00:06:30,765
Baek, listen. You trust me?

86
00:06:31,808 --> 00:06:33,559
Of course, sir, completely.

87
00:06:33,560 --> 00:06:36,103
Good. Trust only me.

88
00:06:36,104 --> 00:06:38,355
One day, I'll end all of this.

89
00:06:38,356 --> 00:06:40,317
That's the only way we'll survive.

90
00:06:41,234 --> 00:06:43,153
I don't know what you mean by that.

91
00:06:45,655 --> 00:06:49,451
"Life's a long journey.
It's so easy to be led astray.

92
00:06:51,369 --> 00:06:53,747
But if a man's determined
to walk his path,

93
00:06:54,539 --> 00:06:56,874
any storm can be weathered.

94
00:06:56,875 --> 00:06:58,585
He'll make his own way."

95
00:07:04,132 --> 00:07:05,383
Have a good day.

96
00:07:13,224 --> 00:07:15,435
Ah, good aftern… What the…

97
00:07:18,855 --> 00:07:21,441
Deputy Director Baek, good afternoon.

98
00:07:21,941 --> 00:07:26,029
Major General Hwang Daesik,
leader of the Military Security Command.

99
00:07:27,030 --> 00:07:30,074
He's known Cheon Seokjung,
the president's favorite advisor,

100
00:07:30,075 --> 00:07:32,701
since their days
at the Korean Military Academy.

101
00:07:32,702 --> 00:07:36,706
But even so, Hwang's been gunning
for Cheon's position for a long time.

102
00:07:38,833 --> 00:07:40,668
Are you here for the president?

103
00:07:40,669 --> 00:07:42,544
I have something I need to report.

104
00:07:45,090 --> 00:07:46,424
Busan keeping you busy lately?

105
00:07:47,258 --> 00:07:51,345
Those bastards. They love to riot
like animals, that's all it is.

106
00:07:51,346 --> 00:07:54,724
After everything the president's done
to better this country,

107
00:07:55,308 --> 00:07:59,144
suddenly a bunch of ungrateful protestors
are whining about terms limits.

108
00:07:59,145 --> 00:08:02,231
And no mention of Kim Ilsung
who's been making himself a god

109
00:08:02,232 --> 00:08:03,942
for the last 30 years.

110
00:08:04,651 --> 00:08:06,151
Democracy?

111
00:08:06,152 --> 00:08:08,862
Do these morons even know
what that word means?

112
00:08:08,863 --> 00:08:10,739
Pampered sons of bitches.

113
00:08:10,740 --> 00:08:14,077
Why don't we just round them up quick
and lop off their heads one by one?

114
00:08:17,038 --> 00:08:18,957
Why don't you and I get a drink sometime?

115
00:08:19,958 --> 00:08:21,458
Why not tonight?

116
00:08:21,459 --> 00:08:23,253
First round's on me.

117
00:08:23,878 --> 00:08:27,507
- Sorry, tonight is no good.
- Ah.

118
00:08:28,550 --> 00:08:30,009
Well, I'm gonna hold you to it.

119
00:08:32,721 --> 00:08:35,473
I'll see you around, Mr. Baek.

120
00:08:42,230 --> 00:08:45,108
That little bastard.
I should just…

121
00:08:50,697 --> 00:08:51,698
Geez.

122
00:08:53,199 --> 00:08:55,702
Hwang Daesik went
to the president's office?

123
00:08:56,953 --> 00:08:59,830
Yes. It seems the president's been
taking an interest in him lately.

124
00:08:59,831 --> 00:09:01,623
CHIEF OF STAFF TO THE PRESIDENT
CHEON SEOKJUNG

125
00:09:01,624 --> 00:09:03,417
Inviting him to drinks and all that.

126
00:09:03,418 --> 00:09:05,420
Wow, that jackass.

127
00:09:09,257 --> 00:09:10,633
Baek, I think…

128
00:09:12,093 --> 00:09:14,387
…we should teach that prick
a lesson while we can.

129
00:09:16,473 --> 00:09:17,891
What do you have in mind?

130
00:09:19,184 --> 00:09:20,769
Why don't you come up with something?

131
00:09:21,811 --> 00:09:23,563
We need to humble him…

132
00:09:24,355 --> 00:09:26,775
before he gets too big for his britches.

133
00:09:27,400 --> 00:09:30,527
Chief Cheon has wielded
absolute power for over a decade,

134
00:09:30,528 --> 00:09:34,531
but even so, he's always
playing second fiddle to the president.

135
00:09:34,532 --> 00:09:36,700
By the way…

136
00:09:36,701 --> 00:09:38,911
…you know how disappointed
the president was

137
00:09:38,912 --> 00:09:40,121
with the last election, right?

138
00:09:41,372 --> 00:09:43,665
Are you talking about the campaign funds?

139
00:09:46,669 --> 00:09:50,215
This time we need to make sure
we have a sizeable war chest.

140
00:09:51,674 --> 00:09:55,677
Sir, I gathered all the resources
I could back then.

141
00:09:55,678 --> 00:09:56,888
Kitae, listen.

142
00:09:58,181 --> 00:10:00,516
I'm not making this request
out of self-interest.

143
00:10:01,893 --> 00:10:05,230
This is all about
planting enough allies, all right?

144
00:10:07,315 --> 00:10:10,193
We need people
in the National Assembly. Hey.

145
00:10:12,862 --> 00:10:15,614
You know why the president
favors Daesik these days?

146
00:10:17,534 --> 00:10:20,703
He tests your loyalty from time to time,
that much I know.

147
00:10:21,996 --> 00:10:23,413
So maybe…

148
00:10:23,414 --> 00:10:26,334
he's trying to toughen you up
and make your skin thicker

149
00:10:27,210 --> 00:10:29,336
before he steps down
and hands his seat to you.

150
00:10:35,718 --> 00:10:39,055
Kitae, Kitae…

151
00:10:42,183 --> 00:10:44,477
You still don't know him at all.

152
00:10:46,354 --> 00:10:50,567
That man has absolutely
no intention of stepping down. Ever.

153
00:10:52,485 --> 00:10:53,820
Don't you get it?

154
00:10:56,239 --> 00:10:57,823
It's because of me.

155
00:10:57,824 --> 00:11:01,411
He's got Hwang Daesik
glued to his hip to keep me in check.

156
00:11:04,122 --> 00:11:05,874
His time's running out, though.

157
00:11:09,043 --> 00:11:10,920
He's not as sharp as he was.

158
00:11:20,805 --> 00:11:22,056
Tell me, Kihun.

159
00:11:22,724 --> 00:11:23,808
Yes, sir.

160
00:11:25,101 --> 00:11:27,145
You've been working with me how long now?

161
00:11:27,812 --> 00:11:30,106
Seven or eight years, I think?

162
00:11:31,441 --> 00:11:33,109
Ever since you moved to Seoul.

163
00:11:34,027 --> 00:11:36,571
Your accent's just as obvious
as it was then.

164
00:11:37,405 --> 00:11:40,283
I've been doing my best, sir.
Is it that easy to tell?

165
00:11:41,326 --> 00:11:43,202
I mean, what do you think?

166
00:11:43,203 --> 00:11:44,787
I'm sorry, sir. I'll try harder.

167
00:11:45,663 --> 00:11:47,123
That's not why I asked.

168
00:11:48,958 --> 00:11:51,210
When do the materials from Taiwan arrive?

169
00:11:51,211 --> 00:11:52,754
Should be here by Sunday, sir.

170
00:11:54,964 --> 00:11:56,840
Make sure to run the lab
day and night

171
00:11:56,841 --> 00:11:58,634
to hit the volume we need.

172
00:11:58,635 --> 00:11:59,844
Understood.

173
00:12:04,265 --> 00:12:05,433
By the way, sir,

174
00:12:06,392 --> 00:12:10,605
do you mind if…
I ask you something about the business?

175
00:12:11,272 --> 00:12:12,439
What is it?

176
00:12:12,440 --> 00:12:14,150
Well, wouldn't we…

177
00:12:14,901 --> 00:12:16,819
wouldn't we increase profits…

178
00:12:17,362 --> 00:12:19,614
if we sold our product here in Korea too?

179
00:12:21,199 --> 00:12:23,200
Exports are important,
but the local market--

180
00:12:23,201 --> 00:12:25,536
- Kihun.
- Uh, yes, sir?

181
00:12:26,287 --> 00:12:29,582
If you don't want to die,
focus on driving.

182
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:32,126
Yes, I apologize.

183
00:12:37,840 --> 00:12:40,635
Why would we push drugs
in this beautiful country?

184
00:12:41,594 --> 00:12:42,887
Don't forget…

185
00:12:45,181 --> 00:12:47,391
what we do is for patriotism.

186
00:12:47,392 --> 00:12:48,642
For our nation.

187
00:12:48,643 --> 00:12:50,520
Yes, of course. Our nation.

188
00:12:59,988 --> 00:13:01,572
What a gorgeous day.

189
00:13:40,737 --> 00:13:43,531
Well, well, well. Here we are.
That was quick.

190
00:13:44,574 --> 00:13:46,825
Bring it this way! More, more.

191
00:13:46,826 --> 00:13:48,703
- Changbae.
- Yeah?

192
00:13:49,203 --> 00:13:51,330
Can you hear the sound
of money rolling in?

193
00:13:51,956 --> 00:13:54,083
Oh, yeah.
I hear it loud and clear.

194
00:13:54,751 --> 00:13:57,545
Pick up the pace! Move it!

195
00:13:58,296 --> 00:14:01,549
OSAKA, JAPAN

196
00:14:03,009 --> 00:14:05,135
Thank you for coming.

197
00:14:05,136 --> 00:14:09,432
There's one simple reason
I called you all here today.

198
00:14:10,933 --> 00:14:13,061
As you all know by now…

199
00:14:14,812 --> 00:14:17,523
my health is failing rather quickly.

200
00:14:18,649 --> 00:14:20,068
Which means that…

201
00:14:20,902 --> 00:14:24,030
remaining in this position
would only reflect…

202
00:14:25,281 --> 00:14:27,116
my own arrogance.

203
00:14:27,825 --> 00:14:28,826
No…

204
00:14:30,536 --> 00:14:33,873
More like excessive greed on my part.

205
00:14:34,415 --> 00:14:35,833
Please, Kumicho.

206
00:14:36,751 --> 00:14:38,753
I urge you to reconsider.

207
00:14:39,921 --> 00:14:41,631
Please reconsider!

208
00:14:42,215 --> 00:14:45,675
Choi Yuji has been
biding her time with her head down

209
00:14:45,676 --> 00:14:47,719
and her claws retracted.

210
00:14:47,720 --> 00:14:49,806
She's waited a while for this moment.

211
00:14:50,598 --> 00:14:52,100
The Ikeda clan…

212
00:14:53,684 --> 00:14:57,355
must not take its current prosperity
for granted.

213
00:14:58,064 --> 00:14:59,774
No complacency.

214
00:15:03,528 --> 00:15:05,613
We must keep rebuilding…

215
00:15:06,864 --> 00:15:11,201
through strong reforms
that bolster the foundation we built.

216
00:15:11,202 --> 00:15:13,245
At the next general meeting,

217
00:15:13,246 --> 00:15:15,665
I will announce my successor,

218
00:15:16,666 --> 00:15:19,293
and my decision will be final.

219
00:15:20,586 --> 00:15:23,380
But no matter
how shrewd and capable she is,

220
00:15:23,381 --> 00:15:26,633
clan leadership would
never willingly accept

221
00:15:26,634 --> 00:15:30,054
a young female Zainichi
as the official successor.

222
00:15:30,930 --> 00:15:32,223
Understood, sir.

223
00:15:33,182 --> 00:15:35,852
If that's what our kumicho
intends for the future…

224
00:15:37,353 --> 00:15:39,981
we will follow you and obey your will.

225
00:15:40,565 --> 00:15:42,233
We will follow it!

226
00:15:43,401 --> 00:15:46,695
If she has any hope
of claiming that seat and rising to power,

227
00:15:46,696 --> 00:15:50,449
her first step is to overcome
this man: Kimura Yoichi.

228
00:15:54,328 --> 00:15:55,829
You wanted to talk?

229
00:15:55,830 --> 00:15:57,373
I'll get straight to the point.

230
00:15:58,374 --> 00:16:01,294
I want your assistance
with the succession, Harimoto.

231
00:16:03,296 --> 00:16:05,755
Kimura's conservative and old-fashioned.

232
00:16:05,756 --> 00:16:09,635
Under him, the clan will stagnate.
Who knows, it may even wither away.

233
00:16:10,970 --> 00:16:12,597
You know that, don't you?

234
00:16:14,307 --> 00:16:15,808
Well, the fact remains.

235
00:16:16,392 --> 00:16:19,562
It's very possible
that your father will choose him.

236
00:16:21,814 --> 00:16:23,649
Don't worry. Leave that to me.

237
00:16:24,358 --> 00:16:28,404
The real question is,
what happens in a power vacuum?

238
00:16:30,489 --> 00:16:33,159
Harimoto, if you and I were
to collaborate,

239
00:16:33,910 --> 00:16:35,828
don't you think we might prevail?

240
00:16:42,251 --> 00:16:46,839
I heard your brother was
arrested in Korea for foreign espionage.

241
00:16:48,633 --> 00:16:51,469
You know I have ties
with the KCIA, don't you?

242
00:16:52,678 --> 00:16:56,224
If you want… I'll make sure he gets out.

243
00:16:59,560 --> 00:17:02,563
In Korea, espionage
gets you the death penalty.

244
00:17:04,232 --> 00:17:08,402
So, then, will you really take over
this clan as kumicho?

245
00:17:15,826 --> 00:17:19,205
Yuji's lifelong dream has
been to lead the clan as kumicho.

246
00:17:20,665 --> 00:17:23,042
She'd do anything to be in control.

247
00:17:25,378 --> 00:17:27,879
Professor Jang Gyeongsik?

248
00:17:27,880 --> 00:17:30,341
He's the brother
of our regional boss, Harimoto.

249
00:17:31,050 --> 00:17:32,843
I mentioned him before, right?

250
00:17:33,844 --> 00:17:35,555
He runs our Tokyo operation.

251
00:17:36,931 --> 00:17:38,849
He's a Zainichi, like me.

252
00:17:40,017 --> 00:17:42,645
Kimura's one of the old guard,
from the main family…

253
00:17:43,604 --> 00:17:45,981
but Harimoto would be a big help to me.

254
00:17:45,982 --> 00:17:47,733
Kimura could be swayed by that.

255
00:17:48,359 --> 00:17:50,944
After all, Harimoto has
a major stake in the clan,

256
00:17:50,945 --> 00:17:52,612
and his influence runs deep.

257
00:17:52,613 --> 00:17:54,739
What exactly do you need from me, then?

258
00:17:57,243 --> 00:18:01,663
Professor Jang Gyeongsik went
to Korea to visit his ancestral graves,

259
00:18:01,664 --> 00:18:03,373
and got himself arrested.

260
00:18:03,374 --> 00:18:04,375
For espionage.

261
00:18:05,042 --> 00:18:07,168
So you're asking me to get him out.

262
00:18:07,169 --> 00:18:08,503
DEPUTY DIRECTOR BAEK KITAE

263
00:18:08,504 --> 00:18:10,298
Think you could pull some strings?

264
00:18:11,048 --> 00:18:12,800
And if I do? What then?

265
00:18:15,761 --> 00:18:17,972
They won't have to announce a successor.

266
00:18:22,184 --> 00:18:24,769
And I can help my father get some rest.

267
00:18:39,160 --> 00:18:43,330
BUSAN, KOREA

268
00:18:59,597 --> 00:19:01,766
You know, I expected it
to be more chaotic.

269
00:19:02,391 --> 00:19:04,018
Heard they burned down a TV station.

270
00:19:05,019 --> 00:19:06,020
You're right.

271
00:19:06,854 --> 00:19:07,855
It is quiet.

272
00:19:08,689 --> 00:19:11,275
What's with the traffic?
Was there an accident?

273
00:19:14,654 --> 00:19:16,738
-  Over there! They're coming!
-  Whoa.

274
00:19:16,739 --> 00:19:19,241
What's going on?

275
00:19:28,042 --> 00:19:29,417
Whoa.

276
00:19:32,046 --> 00:19:33,130
Get off him!

277
00:19:34,173 --> 00:19:35,466
Oh, geez.

278
00:19:48,312 --> 00:19:51,981
You crazy bitch!
All right. That's it. You're dead.

279
00:20:11,544 --> 00:20:13,670
KCIA BUSAN BRANCH

280
00:20:37,278 --> 00:20:38,654
Hold still!

281
00:20:41,657 --> 00:20:43,242
No, please, don't!

282
00:20:44,827 --> 00:20:46,327
No, please, please!

283
00:20:56,005 --> 00:20:57,088
Hey!

284
00:20:59,925 --> 00:21:01,051
Sir.

285
00:21:24,575 --> 00:21:28,621
Deputy Director.
I can't imagine you have much free time.

286
00:21:29,163 --> 00:21:32,750
So what brings you down to Busan, sir?

287
00:21:33,918 --> 00:21:36,169
You really don't have to be polite,
it's just us.

288
00:21:36,170 --> 00:21:37,838
The formality's uncomfortable.

289
00:21:38,506 --> 00:21:40,715
Well, I didn't want
to be inappropriate, sir.

290
00:21:40,716 --> 00:21:43,134
I'm just a lowly branch director general,

291
00:21:43,135 --> 00:21:45,262
and you're the KCIA's second-in-command.

292
00:21:46,180 --> 00:21:48,224
So I can't really be candid unless…

293
00:21:48,933 --> 00:21:50,226
you want me to.

294
00:21:51,227 --> 00:21:52,728
And it sounds like you do?

295
00:21:54,730 --> 00:21:56,106
Don't you?

296
00:21:57,817 --> 00:21:58,818
You got a toupee?

297
00:21:59,902 --> 00:22:01,070
So you noticed?

298
00:22:03,572 --> 00:22:05,950
Can't keep my damn hair for some reason.

299
00:22:06,909 --> 00:22:08,202
I think it's this job.

300
00:22:09,411 --> 00:22:10,912
Director Hwang went bald too.

301
00:22:10,913 --> 00:22:11,996
DIRECTOR GENERAL PYO HAKSU

302
00:22:11,997 --> 00:22:13,499
But you haven't.

303
00:22:15,334 --> 00:22:17,002
Why aren't you losing any?

304
00:22:17,837 --> 00:22:19,588
That'd be a question for your father.

305
00:22:20,381 --> 00:22:22,800
My old man? Right.

306
00:22:23,759 --> 00:22:25,386
What's this job got to do with it?

307
00:22:26,595 --> 00:22:27,847
It's all genetics.

308
00:22:29,098 --> 00:22:31,140
Just have to get lucky at birth, I guess.

309
00:22:31,141 --> 00:22:33,352
I saw quite a scene on the drive in.

310
00:22:35,145 --> 00:22:36,354
What's the status?

311
00:22:36,355 --> 00:22:37,982
It doesn't look good.

312
00:22:38,732 --> 00:22:40,234
Masan's a wreck too.

313
00:22:42,236 --> 00:22:44,446
There's no guarantee
it won't spread to Seoul.

314
00:22:45,447 --> 00:22:47,658
Thing is, the president's
overstayed his welcome.

315
00:22:48,826 --> 00:22:52,037
You're being disrespectful.
What's your deal?

316
00:22:52,705 --> 00:22:54,163
Don't you think he deserves it?

317
00:22:54,164 --> 00:22:56,083
You little shit.

318
00:22:57,418 --> 00:22:58,878
Watch your mouth.

319
00:23:00,129 --> 00:23:01,255
Yes, sir.

320
00:23:13,350 --> 00:23:15,185
You've rounded up a sizable collection.

321
00:23:17,354 --> 00:23:21,191
What can I say? Commies are coming out
of the damn woodwork these days.

322
00:23:24,320 --> 00:23:26,405
Or you're creating them outta thin air.

323
00:23:28,490 --> 00:23:30,033
Well, you know how it is.

324
00:23:30,034 --> 00:23:33,703
The president needs
to see numbers to be persuaded,

325
00:23:33,704 --> 00:23:37,207
especially since he favors the MSC
over the KCIA lately.

326
00:23:37,833 --> 00:23:41,127
Those bastards just couldn't
keep their noses out of anything.

327
00:23:42,838 --> 00:23:44,715
You know what the hardest part is?

328
00:23:45,507 --> 00:23:47,801
You have to keep changing the narratives.

329
00:23:49,386 --> 00:23:52,013
Otherwise, people get bored
and lose interest.

330
00:23:52,014 --> 00:23:53,932
So hire a novelist or something.

331
00:23:53,933 --> 00:23:55,392
I already have, actually.

332
00:23:59,313 --> 00:24:00,356
So what is it?

333
00:24:01,231 --> 00:24:02,441
Why are you here?

334
00:24:05,152 --> 00:24:07,196
I can't get into the details.

335
00:24:09,865 --> 00:24:11,574
Here, this man.

336
00:24:11,575 --> 00:24:12,909
I'm gonna need him, okay?

337
00:24:12,910 --> 00:24:13,993
HANDLER
JANG GYEONGSIK

338
00:24:25,381 --> 00:24:26,548
Who's Jang Gyeongsik?

339
00:24:27,299 --> 00:24:28,300
Hold up your hand.

340
00:24:30,678 --> 00:24:32,471
Who's Jang Gyeongsik?

341
00:24:33,806 --> 00:24:34,807
Raise your hand if it's you.

342
00:24:36,141 --> 00:24:37,684
- Yes?
-  Get him.

343
00:24:38,852 --> 00:24:41,771
Koreans born and raised in Japan
could barely understand,

344
00:24:41,772 --> 00:24:44,899
let alone resist,
South Korea's harsh anti-communist laws.

345
00:24:44,900 --> 00:24:46,234
Get the cuffs!

346
00:24:46,235 --> 00:24:48,361
Many of them
barely spoke Korean at all,

347
00:24:48,362 --> 00:24:52,115
which made them easy targets
in the KCIA and the MSC's quest

348
00:24:52,116 --> 00:24:55,034
to frame unsuspecting expats
for espionage.

349
00:24:55,035 --> 00:24:58,204
Catching spies brought reward money,
professional perks,

350
00:24:58,205 --> 00:25:02,041
special promotions,
even the president's personal favor.

351
00:25:02,042 --> 00:25:06,754
So, naturally, everyone in the government
became obsessed with hunting them down.

352
00:25:10,843 --> 00:25:12,386
You want him released?

353
00:25:16,265 --> 00:25:17,516
Bold move.

354
00:25:18,142 --> 00:25:19,851
You're not worried about the director?

355
00:25:19,852 --> 00:25:21,310
Are you worried about it?

356
00:25:21,311 --> 00:25:24,648
Cho's pretty much finished, but… even so.

357
00:25:25,274 --> 00:25:26,859
Well…

358
00:25:27,860 --> 00:25:29,820
…can you release this guy or not?

359
00:25:32,072 --> 00:25:34,949
You give an order, I follow it.

360
00:25:34,950 --> 00:25:37,076
I'm just a humble branch director general.

361
00:25:46,170 --> 00:25:47,921
By the way,

362
00:25:48,714 --> 00:25:50,674
this stuff's all over Busan right now.

363
00:25:59,099 --> 00:26:01,560
I thought you said
you were only planning to export.

364
00:26:02,644 --> 00:26:04,480
That you wouldn't push it in Korea.

365
00:26:09,943 --> 00:26:12,237
- You found this here in the city?
- Mm-hmm.

366
00:26:13,405 --> 00:26:16,742
There was a woman who used to work
under Jang Geonyoung, remember her?

367
00:26:17,493 --> 00:26:18,910
Oh Yejin.

368
00:26:18,911 --> 00:26:21,662
She's a prosecutor
at the Busan District Office now.

369
00:26:21,663 --> 00:26:23,665
She's desperate to catch people
who sell that.

370
00:26:25,542 --> 00:26:28,295
Word is she's a lunatic, too.
Just like Geonyoung.

371
00:26:28,879 --> 00:26:31,215
She'll move heaven and earth
to get the job done.

372
00:26:37,471 --> 00:26:38,931
Oh, yeah.

373
00:26:39,723 --> 00:26:42,643
That's the number one product
going around these days.

374
00:26:43,685 --> 00:26:45,979
Usually gets exported straight to Tokyo.

375
00:26:46,814 --> 00:26:51,110
Once you get a taste of it,
nothing else hits the same.

376
00:26:55,030 --> 00:26:56,281
So, uh…

377
00:26:57,282 --> 00:26:59,827
how come you're here all alone today,
Miss Oh?

378
00:27:01,537 --> 00:27:02,996
My guys are outside.

379
00:27:03,497 --> 00:27:04,790
They were just in the way.

380
00:27:06,708 --> 00:27:07,876
What about the rest?

381
00:27:10,129 --> 00:27:12,296
How much do you need?

382
00:27:12,297 --> 00:27:13,924
I need all of it.

383
00:27:14,424 --> 00:27:15,467
As much as you've got.

384
00:27:18,887 --> 00:27:20,430
I'm not sure you can handle that.

385
00:27:23,559 --> 00:27:25,686
Look, are we gonna make this deal or not?

386
00:27:29,356 --> 00:27:31,566
How bad do you want it?

387
00:27:31,567 --> 00:27:32,651
I'm up for anything.

388
00:27:33,944 --> 00:27:35,237
Yeah, me too.

389
00:27:40,868 --> 00:27:41,869
Well, come on, then.

390
00:27:48,917 --> 00:27:51,878
You wanna do it now?
With the boys watching?

391
00:27:51,879 --> 00:27:53,005
Why not?

392
00:27:54,047 --> 00:27:56,300
Always better with an audience.

393
00:27:57,092 --> 00:27:59,511
Oh, wait… are you serious?

394
00:28:02,097 --> 00:28:04,599
All right. Yeah. Uh…

395
00:28:04,600 --> 00:28:06,434
Aw, yeah, great.

396
00:28:06,435 --> 00:28:08,562
What are you idiots looking at?
Close your eyes.

397
00:28:09,563 --> 00:28:10,980
Right, here we go.

398
00:28:12,566 --> 00:28:14,358
Wh-wh-what are you doing? Come on.

399
00:28:14,359 --> 00:28:16,111
Don't be such a tease.

400
00:28:18,572 --> 00:28:21,032
Come on, I can't take it!

401
00:28:21,033 --> 00:28:23,827
All right, let's get down to business.

402
00:28:26,705 --> 00:28:29,040
Hey! What the hell?

403
00:28:29,041 --> 00:28:30,917
Goddamn it!

404
00:28:46,975 --> 00:28:47,976
Come here!

405
00:28:48,644 --> 00:28:51,437
Whoa, what are you doing?
Hey, stop it! No!

406
00:28:51,438 --> 00:28:53,398
Miss Oh, you're not allowed to--

407
00:29:02,240 --> 00:29:03,574
Who are you really?

408
00:29:03,575 --> 00:29:07,328
I'm Prosecutor Oh Yejin
from the Busan District Office,

409
00:29:07,329 --> 00:29:09,498
you drug-dealing sack of shit!

410
00:29:10,123 --> 00:29:11,582
One…

411
00:29:11,583 --> 00:29:12,667
Shut up, idiot.

412
00:29:12,668 --> 00:29:13,793
…two…

413
00:29:13,794 --> 00:29:15,087
- Cut the shit, all right?
- …three,

414
00:29:15,671 --> 00:29:18,381
- and four.
- Hey, asshole, stay down on your knees.

415
00:29:18,382 --> 00:29:20,884
Shut up. Look at me, you prick.

416
00:29:21,510 --> 00:29:23,594
Okay. Where'd you get the drugs?

417
00:29:26,139 --> 00:29:27,306
Listen, Kim.

418
00:29:27,307 --> 00:29:30,851
You go back to jail, you'll be doing
a mandatory minimum of ten years.

419
00:29:30,852 --> 00:29:32,562
Understand?

420
00:29:34,106 --> 00:29:36,107
Just for pushing a little meth?

421
00:29:36,108 --> 00:29:38,526
You're pulling my leg, aren't you?

422
00:29:38,527 --> 00:29:40,403
- Nope.
- Argh, shit!

423
00:29:40,404 --> 00:29:41,529
Damn it!

424
00:29:41,530 --> 00:29:42,613
- You know…
- Ow.

425
00:29:42,614 --> 00:29:45,617
…I busted my ass for ten years
to become a prosecutor.

426
00:29:46,660 --> 00:29:47,952
Why?

427
00:29:47,953 --> 00:29:51,622
To throw little scumbags
like you into prison forever.

428
00:29:54,835 --> 00:29:56,878
So I'd stake my badge on this.

429
00:29:57,546 --> 00:29:59,464
You're so screwed.

430
00:30:00,215 --> 00:30:01,633
So what's it gonna be?

431
00:30:02,342 --> 00:30:05,219
Start talking
and do a year in county jail,

432
00:30:05,220 --> 00:30:07,430
or get sent to prison for a decade?

433
00:30:08,557 --> 00:30:11,058
You really wanna deal with
the other inmates every day?

434
00:30:13,895 --> 00:30:15,731
A year.

435
00:30:16,732 --> 00:30:19,859
- You give me your word?
- Oh, yeah, I got you.

436
00:30:19,860 --> 00:30:21,402
It's a deal then.

437
00:30:21,403 --> 00:30:23,613
So, who's supplying you?

438
00:30:25,991 --> 00:30:29,827
Changbae. He runs a lab up in Seoul.
That's where they make this stuff.

439
00:30:29,828 --> 00:30:32,371
And, man, it's, uh… just…

440
00:30:32,372 --> 00:30:34,415
It's killer. And normally they…

441
00:30:34,416 --> 00:30:38,462
they only export it to Japan, you usually
can't find it anywhere in Korea.

442
00:30:39,129 --> 00:30:41,130
But he must've needed the cash.

443
00:30:41,131 --> 00:30:43,007
So he came right to me.

444
00:30:43,008 --> 00:30:44,300
"Changbae"?

445
00:30:44,301 --> 00:30:46,428
Yeah. Park Changbae.

446
00:30:47,763 --> 00:30:49,848
Park Changbae, huh?

447
00:30:55,395 --> 00:30:57,689
You're drinking before
the sun's even gone down?

448
00:30:58,273 --> 00:30:59,274
Huh?

449
00:30:59,900 --> 00:31:01,610
You know how bad that is for you?

450
00:31:03,987 --> 00:31:05,363
Come on.

451
00:31:13,163 --> 00:31:16,833
Oh, whoa, whoa, whoa. Easy.
You're breaking everything.

452
00:31:19,127 --> 00:31:21,463
- What are you doing?
- I'd love…

453
00:31:22,798 --> 00:31:23,799
a little refill, please.

454
00:31:27,594 --> 00:31:29,638
You're gonna put your stomach
through hell.

455
00:31:30,680 --> 00:31:32,641
Oh, whatever.

456
00:31:33,183 --> 00:31:34,558
All right.

457
00:31:37,020 --> 00:31:39,981
How about some food? Oh, what…

458
00:31:43,652 --> 00:31:45,237
What's up with you?

459
00:31:45,862 --> 00:31:47,405
Uh, what's happening?

460
00:31:48,824 --> 00:31:51,368
You wanna?

461
00:31:52,369 --> 00:31:53,494
What are you saying?

462
00:31:55,413 --> 00:31:57,499
- What do you think?
- Ah! Shit.

463
00:32:00,085 --> 00:32:02,587
Dumbass. Your face!

464
00:32:04,339 --> 00:32:05,882
Oh! Uh…

465
00:32:07,926 --> 00:32:10,887
Oh, my gosh.
I wasn't expecting you, Kitae.

466
00:32:12,180 --> 00:32:13,556
Nobody else here?

467
00:32:13,557 --> 00:32:15,474
No. We finished all the shipments,

468
00:32:15,475 --> 00:32:17,477
so everyone got to head out early.

469
00:32:25,986 --> 00:32:29,321
Soyeong, go get ready for the memorial.
Kihyun's going too.

470
00:32:29,322 --> 00:32:30,323
Oh.

471
00:32:31,158 --> 00:32:34,118
All right, I'll go. What about you?

472
00:32:34,119 --> 00:32:36,329
I need to talk to Changbae first.

473
00:32:43,170 --> 00:32:44,379
Okay.

474
00:32:50,218 --> 00:32:52,220
-  Have a seat.
- Right, sure.

475
00:33:05,775 --> 00:33:06,776
Changbae.

476
00:33:07,360 --> 00:33:08,361
Yes, sir?

477
00:33:10,071 --> 00:33:13,783
What do you think is the most
essential virtue a person should have?

478
00:33:16,286 --> 00:33:17,329
Love, I guess?

479
00:33:18,079 --> 00:33:20,415
Love.

480
00:33:22,834 --> 00:33:24,878
Right, love is important, sure.

481
00:33:26,546 --> 00:33:28,048
Wanna know what I'd pick?

482
00:33:29,257 --> 00:33:31,134
Shame would be my answer.

483
00:33:32,093 --> 00:33:33,636
Shame? Really?

484
00:33:33,637 --> 00:33:36,806
There's no one I hate more
than a shameless person.

485
00:33:38,975 --> 00:33:41,603
Someone that's blithe
and careless in everything they do.

486
00:33:45,357 --> 00:33:47,608
A shameless guy is always deferent.

487
00:33:47,609 --> 00:33:50,946
He'll smile and nod
and swear he'll do anything for you.

488
00:33:51,655 --> 00:33:52,947
But when it really counts,

489
00:33:52,948 --> 00:33:55,491
he'll stick a knife in your back
like it's nothing.

490
00:33:57,619 --> 00:33:58,870
That's what it means…

491
00:34:01,957 --> 00:34:03,792
to be shameless in this world.

492
00:34:06,253 --> 00:34:07,921
And if you have no shame…

493
00:34:08,630 --> 00:34:11,507
you're no different
than an animal in the wild.

494
00:34:11,508 --> 00:34:12,509
Don't you think?

495
00:34:22,519 --> 00:34:24,187
You skimming our stuff?

496
00:34:27,565 --> 00:34:29,984
What? I didn't take any product.

497
00:34:32,153 --> 00:34:33,488
Look, sir, I'm sorry.

498
00:34:34,155 --> 00:34:37,408
I'm not sure we can keep working
together if you're going to do this.

499
00:34:37,409 --> 00:34:40,786
I'm telling you, I didn't do anything.
All right?

500
00:34:40,787 --> 00:34:42,663
Trust me, okay?

501
00:34:42,664 --> 00:34:44,164
Just please, don't!

502
00:34:44,165 --> 00:34:46,041
You're pushing the product in Busan.

503
00:34:46,042 --> 00:34:48,210
I didn't do that. I wouldn't betray you.

504
00:34:50,297 --> 00:34:52,549
I didn't skim product off the top, sir.

505
00:34:53,925 --> 00:34:56,678
I didn't, I swear on my life.
Please believe me.

506
00:35:04,227 --> 00:35:05,979
So you're saying it wasn't you?

507
00:35:12,819 --> 00:35:16,323
Yes, it really wasn't me, okay?

508
00:35:23,455 --> 00:35:24,623
Clean this up.

509
00:35:26,458 --> 00:35:27,542
Yes, sir. I'm on it.

510
00:35:30,462 --> 00:35:32,630
MILITARY SECURITY COMMAND

511
00:35:54,861 --> 00:35:56,738
- Wanna have a cigarette?
- Sure, sir.

512
00:36:05,038 --> 00:36:06,081
Mmm.

513
00:36:07,666 --> 00:36:08,958
- Mmm, mmm.
- Thanks.

514
00:36:14,005 --> 00:36:15,965
How's the office? Settling in?

515
00:36:16,549 --> 00:36:18,300
Yes, sir. It's perfect.

516
00:36:18,301 --> 00:36:20,886
It was just yesterday you were a captain,

517
00:36:20,887 --> 00:36:23,597
and now you've already
been promoted again. Wow.

518
00:36:23,598 --> 00:36:24,933
Time really flies.

519
00:36:25,600 --> 00:36:28,687
- Well, you played a big part in that.
- Oh, come on, that's not true.

520
00:36:29,396 --> 00:36:30,896
You earned it all yourself.

521
00:36:30,897 --> 00:36:32,899
I don't know…

522
00:36:33,441 --> 00:36:35,819
Didn't you say
you had a memorial service today?

523
00:36:36,611 --> 00:36:37,861
Yes, sir. For my father.

524
00:36:37,862 --> 00:36:40,907
Wrap up and head out.
Why are you still working?

525
00:36:41,491 --> 00:36:44,953
I have a few more things to take care of.
I'll go once I'm finished.

526
00:36:47,288 --> 00:36:48,790
I imagine you'll be

527
00:36:49,624 --> 00:36:51,835
seeing your brother, right?

528
00:36:53,920 --> 00:36:56,380
Yes, sir.

529
00:36:56,381 --> 00:36:58,674
The Busan situation…

530
00:36:58,675 --> 00:37:01,010
…must keep him pretty busy, huh?

531
00:37:03,012 --> 00:37:05,765
Well, I suppose so.

532
00:37:40,759 --> 00:37:41,760
Here.

533
00:37:48,683 --> 00:37:49,767
To your promotion.

534
00:37:49,768 --> 00:37:51,352
Thank you so much.

535
00:37:54,314 --> 00:37:57,941
Our Kihyun's a big man now, huh?
Lieutenant colonel already.

536
00:37:57,942 --> 00:37:59,652
None of your classmates can say that.

537
00:38:00,236 --> 00:38:02,614
Before you know it,
he'll be a general, don't you think?

538
00:38:03,198 --> 00:38:05,365
- It's all because of you.
- Oh, please.

539
00:38:05,366 --> 00:38:07,660
No, I barely lifted a finger.

540
00:38:11,164 --> 00:38:14,417
You know, Kihyun, Kitae pulled
a lot of strings behind the scenes.

541
00:38:15,418 --> 00:38:18,086
We owe everything we have to him,
you know.

542
00:38:18,087 --> 00:38:20,255
This beautiful home, for instance.

543
00:38:20,256 --> 00:38:22,341
You should really come by more often.

544
00:38:22,342 --> 00:38:24,135
- We would love to have you--
- Soyeong.

545
00:38:24,677 --> 00:38:26,095
Your food's getting cold.

546
00:38:29,682 --> 00:38:31,184
Come on, aren't you gonna eat with us?

547
00:38:31,810 --> 00:38:34,019
Do I have to keep feeding you like a baby?

548
00:38:34,020 --> 00:38:36,731
- Say "ah."
- No, I'm too tired right now.

549
00:38:37,649 --> 00:38:40,734
If you finish your dinner,
I'll read you a bedtime story later.

550
00:38:40,735 --> 00:38:41,861
Come on.

551
00:38:43,613 --> 00:38:47,742
Uncle Kihyun, I don't know
what a promotion is.

552
00:38:48,618 --> 00:38:51,036
Hmm. It means I moved up in rank.

553
00:38:51,037 --> 00:38:52,454
I'm a lieutenant colonel now.

554
00:38:52,455 --> 00:38:54,373
What's "rank"?

555
00:38:54,374 --> 00:38:58,293
Well, uh, you moved up
from first grade to second grade, right?

556
00:38:58,294 --> 00:38:59,295
It's like that.

557
00:39:00,463 --> 00:39:04,800
- Oh, so you went up higher?
- Mm-hmm.

558
00:39:04,801 --> 00:39:09,847
Is Uncle Kitae more higher up than you,
or are you more higher up than him now?

559
00:39:09,848 --> 00:39:12,433
He's much higher up than me.

560
00:39:14,644 --> 00:39:17,604
General Hwang been good to you?
Now that you're working for him?

561
00:39:17,605 --> 00:39:18,814
Yes.

562
00:39:18,815 --> 00:39:20,942
Not giving you a hard time
because we're related?

563
00:39:21,568 --> 00:39:22,651
Nobody is.

564
00:39:22,652 --> 00:39:24,654
The colonel's been good to me too.
So, it's been fine.

565
00:39:25,864 --> 00:39:28,198
Ahn Jaeho, right?
Military Academy graduate.

566
00:39:28,199 --> 00:39:29,325
Yes.

567
00:39:31,035 --> 00:39:33,079
I hear
that he's General Hwang's right-hand.

568
00:39:33,746 --> 00:39:34,956
He mention me at all?

569
00:39:36,249 --> 00:39:37,667
I don't believe he has.

570
00:39:38,710 --> 00:39:41,880
Word is Hwang's been
gathering officers around him lately.

571
00:39:43,131 --> 00:39:45,465
He mostly meets with colonels
from the academy.

572
00:39:45,466 --> 00:39:46,758
They drink, play golf.

573
00:39:46,759 --> 00:39:50,179
He's made it clear he's a strong leader,
so lots of people follow him.

574
00:39:51,973 --> 00:39:53,892
Just keep an eye on him, you got that?

575
00:39:54,976 --> 00:39:57,645
Watch who joins his group
and track all his people.

576
00:40:00,231 --> 00:40:01,232
Are you not…

577
00:40:01,983 --> 00:40:03,067
comfortable with that?

578
00:40:04,819 --> 00:40:05,987
No, I'm fine.

579
00:40:08,323 --> 00:40:09,449
Kihyun, look.

580
00:40:10,700 --> 00:40:13,161
You're my brother, hmm?

581
00:40:14,287 --> 00:40:16,414
You know you can't be
in General Hwang's circle.

582
00:40:18,166 --> 00:40:19,500
Of course. I'm aware.

583
00:40:22,962 --> 00:40:26,757
Sorry, but,
who's General Hwang, Uncle Kihyun?

584
00:40:34,724 --> 00:40:35,725
Yes, hello?

585
00:40:36,809 --> 00:40:39,437
- A few more bites. Here.
- Just a minute.

586
00:40:40,188 --> 00:40:42,357
Sorry, but it's Miss Choi.

587
00:40:46,277 --> 00:40:48,738
- I'll take it downstairs.
-  Mmm.

588
00:41:07,423 --> 00:41:08,507
Hi.

589
00:41:08,508 --> 00:41:10,467
How did it go with Professor Jang?

590
00:41:10,468 --> 00:41:11,469
Hold on a minute.

591
00:41:12,095 --> 00:41:14,138
Soyeong, hang up.

592
00:41:19,143 --> 00:41:20,228
We leave tomorrow.

593
00:41:20,770 --> 00:41:22,897
Do you have everything ready?

594
00:41:24,023 --> 00:41:25,441
Don't worry about that.

595
00:41:26,150 --> 00:41:28,111
I just need you to make it on time.

596
00:41:55,179 --> 00:41:56,180
Father.

597
00:41:57,473 --> 00:42:00,518
As for your successor,
have you decided yet?

598
00:42:06,566 --> 00:42:08,443
It's Kimura, isn't it?

599
00:42:14,574 --> 00:42:15,866
So,

600
00:42:15,867 --> 00:42:19,037
you want me to step aside, too,
is that right?

601
00:42:26,419 --> 00:42:28,880
No matter who the successor is,

602
00:42:29,672 --> 00:42:32,175
I still can't leave things to you all yet.

603
00:42:35,428 --> 00:42:37,637
So keep supporting me

604
00:42:37,638 --> 00:42:40,599
and learning from me, hmm?

605
00:42:40,600 --> 00:42:42,852
Stay here, by my side…

606
00:42:46,189 --> 00:42:48,608
the same way you always have.

607
00:42:49,567 --> 00:42:50,860
Hmm?

608
00:42:57,158 --> 00:42:58,576
Yes, I promise.

609
00:42:59,494 --> 00:43:01,870
I'll always do whatever you tell me.

610
00:43:01,871 --> 00:43:02,955
Uh-huh.

611
00:43:07,043 --> 00:43:08,377
I'll go get some tea.

612
00:43:09,170 --> 00:43:11,214
Oh, sure.

613
00:43:26,104 --> 00:43:27,521
As fate would have it,

614
00:43:27,522 --> 00:43:30,899
Chairman Ikeda died of cardiac arrest
at his residence that night.

615
00:43:34,737 --> 00:43:37,573
Yakuza from all across Japan
attended the funeral.

616
00:43:38,199 --> 00:43:41,493
And since the chairman died
without naming a successor,

617
00:43:41,494 --> 00:43:43,954
speculation over
who would fill the power vacuum

618
00:43:43,955 --> 00:43:46,499
became the center
of the mourners' attention.

619
00:44:03,975 --> 00:44:05,059
Okay, Professor.

620
00:44:05,935 --> 00:44:08,729
Everything you saw in Korea?
Forget about it.

621
00:44:09,981 --> 00:44:11,524
Erase it, you understand?

622
00:44:16,320 --> 00:44:17,530
And why don't you…

623
00:44:18,364 --> 00:44:20,449
put in a good word with Harimoto
while you're at it.

624
00:45:38,778 --> 00:45:41,697
That's enough! No more photos.

625
00:46:12,520 --> 00:46:13,728
In the end,

626
00:46:13,729 --> 00:46:16,607
the Ikeda clan decided
to choose the next kumicho by vote.

627
00:46:17,483 --> 00:46:20,611
Choi Yuji secured nine votes
out of the gate.

628
00:46:21,320 --> 00:46:25,074
The question is will Harimoto stand by her
like he promised?

629
00:46:25,783 --> 00:46:28,744
If so, the position would finally be hers.

630
00:46:40,923 --> 00:46:43,009
The voting process is complete.

631
00:46:46,887 --> 00:46:48,973
We will now count the ballots.

632
00:46:54,103 --> 00:46:56,397
It's time.
They're counting ballots.

633
00:47:05,323 --> 00:47:06,324
"Ikeda Yuji."

634
00:47:13,205 --> 00:47:14,206
"Kimura Yoichi."

635
00:47:17,501 --> 00:47:18,502
"Kimura Yoichi."

636
00:47:24,467 --> 00:47:25,468
"Ikeda Yuji."

637
00:47:28,971 --> 00:47:30,264
"Kimura Yoichi."

638
00:47:32,975 --> 00:47:34,143
"Ikeda Yuji."

639
00:47:38,230 --> 00:47:39,315
"Kimura Yoichi."

640
00:47:43,152 --> 00:47:44,153
"Ikeda Yuji."

641
00:47:48,574 --> 00:47:49,575
"Ikeda Yuji."

642
00:47:51,243 --> 00:47:52,244
"Kimura Yoichi."

643
00:47:54,580 --> 00:47:55,581
"Kimura Yoichi."

644
00:47:58,667 --> 00:47:59,668
"Ikeda Yuji."

645
00:48:02,963 --> 00:48:03,964
"Kimura Yoichi."

646
00:48:06,425 --> 00:48:07,468
"Ikeda Yuji."

647
00:48:10,137 --> 00:48:11,554
"Ikeda Yuji."

648
00:48:11,555 --> 00:48:14,642
IKEDA YUJI - KIMURA YOICHI

649
00:48:18,437 --> 00:48:19,772
"Kimura Yoichi."

650
00:48:26,070 --> 00:48:28,364
Kimura Yoichi, ten votes.

651
00:48:28,989 --> 00:48:30,991
Ikeda Yuji, nine votes.

652
00:48:31,617 --> 00:48:33,410
Nineteen votes in total.

653
00:48:33,411 --> 00:48:34,661
According to these results,

654
00:48:34,662 --> 00:48:38,289
Kimura Yoichi is hereby named
the fourth kumicho of the Ikeda clan.

655
00:49:07,445 --> 00:49:10,239
How dare
this Korean mongrel whore…

656
00:49:11,198 --> 00:49:13,784
aim to take full control of our clan.

657
00:49:15,035 --> 00:49:17,455
Go on, drag her out of here before I do.

658
00:50:51,632 --> 00:50:54,050
You bitch! What'd you…

659
00:51:11,151 --> 00:51:13,361
Yuji! Yuji!

660
00:51:20,703 --> 00:51:21,996
Yuji!

661
00:51:25,207 --> 00:51:26,958
Yuji…

662
00:52:33,025 --> 00:52:34,860
Listen, I'm kumicho now.

663
00:52:36,278 --> 00:52:37,446
Are there any objections?

664
00:52:39,198 --> 00:52:40,908
We submit to you!

665
00:52:43,077 --> 00:52:46,496
OCTOBER 26, 1979

666
00:52:46,497 --> 00:52:49,082
Meanwhile,
there was another group gathering

667
00:52:49,083 --> 00:52:51,709
with their eyes
on their own kumicho's seat.

668
00:52:54,880 --> 00:52:57,925
Hey, slow down. Quit drinking so much.

669
00:52:59,802 --> 00:53:01,845
Director Cho, did you make it to Busan?

670
00:53:03,555 --> 00:53:05,223
What did you find out about the protests?

671
00:53:05,224 --> 00:53:08,059
It's just… students and normal people.

672
00:53:09,603 --> 00:53:11,397
They burned down a broadcasting station.

673
00:53:12,064 --> 00:53:13,649
They're not just normal people.

674
00:53:15,067 --> 00:53:16,860
Sir, listen.

675
00:53:17,611 --> 00:53:21,572
We'd better take drastic measures
before these protests get worse.

676
00:53:21,573 --> 00:53:24,450
This is no time to be talking
about martial law.

677
00:53:24,451 --> 00:53:27,787
Busan and Masan aren't islands.
Who says it won't spread to the capital?

678
00:53:27,788 --> 00:53:29,707
I know that!

679
00:53:30,457 --> 00:53:31,833
That's why we need to crush them!

680
00:53:31,834 --> 00:53:34,420
In Cambodia,
they killed three million people!

681
00:53:35,003 --> 00:53:37,130
If we roll armor
over a couple million Reds,

682
00:53:37,131 --> 00:53:38,507
would anyone care?

683
00:53:41,468 --> 00:53:44,470
You crazy son of a bitch,
I'm sick of your bullshit.

684
00:53:44,471 --> 00:53:45,639
What?

685
00:53:50,602 --> 00:53:51,895
You damn lunatic.

686
00:53:52,730 --> 00:53:55,898
Keep talking like that
and you'll be the first to die.

687
00:53:55,899 --> 00:53:58,276
You little…

688
00:54:01,780 --> 00:54:04,574
Director Cho, explain yourself.

689
00:54:04,575 --> 00:54:05,576
Sir, listen.

690
00:54:06,869 --> 00:54:09,203
The more you keep scum like this
by your side,

691
00:54:09,204 --> 00:54:11,165
the sooner this country collapses.

692
00:54:11,749 --> 00:54:12,750
What?

693
00:54:13,333 --> 00:54:15,252
The good of our people should come first.

694
00:54:24,261 --> 00:54:25,304
Look at me.

695
00:54:26,638 --> 00:54:27,848
You wanna be shot?

696
00:54:44,072 --> 00:54:45,073
You have a call, sir.

697
00:55:04,301 --> 00:55:05,302
Sir.

698
00:55:05,886 --> 00:55:07,804
Choi Yuji just made herself the kumicho.

699
00:55:08,347 --> 00:55:10,682
It's not the time for that.
You need to get over here.

700
00:55:11,475 --> 00:55:13,518
I've got a bad feeling.

701
00:55:15,896 --> 00:55:19,148
Cho might be about
to pull something tonight.

702
00:55:19,149 --> 00:55:20,400
Get here now.

703
00:55:22,152 --> 00:55:23,320
I'm on my way.

704
00:55:31,912 --> 00:55:33,162
Gungjeong-dong. Now.

705
00:55:54,184 --> 00:55:57,187
- Oh, shit. What the hell?
-  Wh-what was that?

706
00:56:07,489 --> 00:56:08,657
Wait, sir, be careful.

707
00:56:28,051 --> 00:56:30,095
Damn it! Ah, shit.

708
00:56:31,138 --> 00:56:32,221
Director.

709
00:56:32,222 --> 00:56:34,557
Son of a bitch!

710
00:56:34,558 --> 00:56:36,351
Hey! Bring me your gun!

711
00:56:37,311 --> 00:56:38,812
Ah, shit, come on!

712
00:56:39,896 --> 00:56:41,773
The fucking thing's jammed!

713
00:56:43,317 --> 00:56:46,360
Hey, why are all the lights out?

714
00:56:46,361 --> 00:56:47,362
Sir?

715
00:56:48,322 --> 00:56:50,616
It's pitch black.
How am I supposed to do this?

716
00:56:51,283 --> 00:56:52,659
Please, tell me what's happening, sir.

717
00:56:53,702 --> 00:56:55,119
Stay outside.

718
00:56:55,120 --> 00:56:57,080
I'm gonna finish this once and for all.

719
00:56:58,957 --> 00:57:00,083
Damn it.

720
00:57:04,796 --> 00:57:07,215
Sir, uh… wh-what the hell's happening?

721
00:57:07,883 --> 00:57:10,427
Beats me,
but whatever it is, we're screwed.

722
00:57:15,724 --> 00:57:16,892
Shit.

723
00:57:22,189 --> 00:57:24,982
On October 26th, 1979,

724
00:57:24,983 --> 00:57:28,653
the kumicho, the boss,
the president of South Korea,

725
00:57:28,654 --> 00:57:29,904
died.
